Reference diff: add i686-forestos / x86_64-forestos targets to gcc/config.gcc.

This documents the change build-toolchain.sh applies idempotently (via a
guarded sed insertion just before the `i[34567]86-*-elf*)` case in the big
`case ${target} in` block, ~line 1864 of gcc-13.2.0/gcc/config.gcc).

The Forest-OS targets mirror the bare i386/x86_64 ELF configuration
(newlib-stdint, i386elf.h) and additionally pull in config/forestos.h,
which is installed from patches/gcc/config/forestos.h.

--- a/gcc/config.gcc
+++ b/gcc/config.gcc
@@ (in `case ${target} in`, immediately before the i[34567]86-*-elf*) case)
+i[34567]86-*-forestos*)
+	tm_file="${tm_file} i386/unix.h i386/att.h elfos.h newlib-stdint.h i386/i386elf.h forestos.h"
+	;;
+x86_64-*-forestos*)
+	tm_file="${tm_file} i386/unix.h i386/att.h elfos.h newlib-stdint.h i386/i386elf.h i386/x86-64.h forestos.h"
+	;;
 i[34567]86-*-elf*)
 	tm_file="${tm_file} i386/unix.h i386/att.h elfos.h newlib-stdint.h i386/i386elf.h"
 	;;
 x86_64-*-elf*)
 	tm_file="${tm_file} i386/unix.h i386/att.h elfos.h newlib-stdint.h i386/i386elf.h i386/x86-64.h"
 	;;

Note: cpu_type and --with-abi handling for these triples is already covered
by the generic `i[34567]86-*-* | x86_64-*-*)` cpu block and the
`i[34567]86-*-*)` / `x86_64-*-*)` abi blocks earlier in config.gcc, so no
further edits are required there.
